From 67221e72d50cf15f1c19a889bc6820287b44fd1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhengd-nv <200704041+zhengd-nv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 12:25:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] [Kernel] Add the FlashInfer SM90 MXFP4 x FP8 "humming"
 fused MoE backend

Wires FlashInfer's SM90 humming path (MXFP4 weights, FP8 activations
quantized inside the kernel via pre-MMA E8M0 scale fusion) into the
MXFP4 MoE oracle, so DeepSeek-V4 checkpoints can run it on Hopper.

The weight preprocessing folds the E8M0 scale into an exponent offset
and carries a per-expert fp32 residual, which FlashInferExperts.apply
folds into per-token, expert-contiguous routed scales. Several details
here look simplifiable but silently produce wrong numerics if changed,
so they are commented at the point of use: the 5-slot quant_scales
layout, the gate/up swap without de-interleave, the stable argsort
instead of a boolean mask (which would break cudagraph capture), and
indexing residuals by local expert id under EP.

Validated against a dequantized reference forward on real weights at
ep=1/2/4 (bad_frac=0) and end to end on H20.

Signed-off-by: zhengd-nv <200704041+zhengd-nv@users.noreply.github.com>
