From 728b458340bf7c5902230cc77663f185a9b06544 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhengd-nv <200704041+zhengd-nv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 10:34:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Expose the FlashInfer SM90 humming MoE kernel as
 --moe-backend

Adds "flashinfer_cutlass_humming" to the MoEBackend literal so the
FlashInfer CUTLASS SM90 MXFP4-weight x FP8-activation path can be
selected explicitly. The name collides with the unrelated third-party
"humming" package backend, so the --help text separates the two.

Also fails fast on the two ways the backend can be misdirected: an
explicit request on non-SM90 hardware, and a GPT-OSS row-interleaved
w13 layout, which the humming weight preprocessing would run with the
right shapes but the wrong numerics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: zhengd-nv <200704041+zhengd-nv@users.noreply.github.com>
