Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Probe for the FlashInfer humming MoE kernel before
 selecting it

The humming symbols only exist in flashinfer-python >= 0.6.16, so on an
older install an explicit --moe-backend flashinfer_cutlass_humming used
to surface as an ImportError from inside weight loading. Add
has_flashinfer_humming_moe() and check it where the backend is chosen,
so the failure names the version to install.

The probe looks for the symbols the humming path actually calls rather
than a version, and deliberately does not build on
has_flashinfer_cutlass_fused_moe(): that helper also demands nvfp4 and
TRT-LLM symbols which this path never touches and which are missing from
builds where humming runs correctly.

