Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Hoist per-forward constants out of the humming apply path

The SM90 humming branch rebuilt several constants on every forward: the
epilogue compensation was re-applied to the gathered residuals, and two
temporaries were materialised only to serve as the `other` operand of a
where.

Fold the compensation into the residual tables once, cached rather than
applied in place because g1/g2_alphas are shared with the nvfp4 paths.
Pass scalars to where instead of zeros_like/full_like, and keep a single
ones scalar rather than allocating one per call.

Saves roughly five kernels per MoE layer per step, which at 43 layers is
not nothing on a decode step, and changes no numerics.

