Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:12:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Pass humming residuals per local expert, not per routed
 token

FlashInfer #4431 changed the humming quant-scale contract: slots 1 and 4 are
now [num_local_experts] fp32 arrays and the fused MoE runtime selects each
routed row's residual with the expert-permuted token map it already builds.

The caller therefore stops duplicating that permutation. This drops the
torch.argsort and both gathers, which nsys measured at 27.4 us/layer-step
against 1.6 us for a purpose-built sort kernel, and removes the coupling where
a change to the kernel's internal ordering would silently produce wrong values
here rather than an error. Routing still passes global expert ids; the kernel
maps them to rank-local indices before reading the arrays.

The fixed 2^6 compensation is still the caller's job, so the cached scaled
copies stay.

