From 6c9e3aabf8dba1e1515b654840b8dba5b35eb430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhengd-nv <200704041+zhengd-nv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:05:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Require the per-local-expert humming residual contract

FlashInfer #3738 shipped the SM90 humming kernel with one residual scale per
routed token; #4431 changed it to one per local expert, which is the contract
this backend is written against. Every symbol and keyword the probe looked at
is present in both, so a #3738-only build was selected and then handed the
wrong contract. That usually raises a shape error, but when num_tokens * top_k
equals the local expert count it passes the check and computes silently wrong
results.

#4431 changed no Python signature, so there is nothing to introspect. The
kernel-side shape check that enforces the contract ships as JIT source inside
the wheel, so read that instead, and fail closed if it is not there.

Signed-off-by: zhengd-nv <200704041+zhengd-nv@users.noreply.github.com>
