From ac2c217e40f0ae192b053b729373e02207791b96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhengd-nv <200704041+zhengd-nv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:21:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Name the FlashInfer version the probe actually requires

The probe was extended to reject builds without #4431, but the error it raises
still told the user to install >=0.6.16. That is worse than unhelpful for the
case the check exists for: someone on a build carrying the humming kernel
without #4431 already satisfies it, and someone on 0.6.17 would upgrade within
the line where the kernel is reverted and fail again.

Also fold the four config-surface assertions into one parametrized test and
drop the two that only exercised argparse behaviour shared by every backend
name, so what is left is specific to this change.

